1
00:00:07,125 --> 00:00:10,041
How long are you gonna take eating, huh?

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:12,125
You're an eyesore.

3
00:00:13,125 --> 00:00:16,125
Damn evil-looking brat.

4
00:00:20,125 --> 00:00:22,041
I'm sorry.

5
00:00:22,041 --> 00:00:23,166
I can't hear you!

6
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:27,166
I'm sorry.

7
00:00:27,166 --> 00:00:30,083
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

8
00:00:31,083 --> 00:00:33,041
I'm sorry.

9
00:00:36,083 --> 00:00:39,000
...you. I'll...

10
00:00:49,083 --> 00:00:51,041
Hey, stop!

11
00:00:51,083 --> 00:00:53,083
Oyamada-kun, give that back.

12
00:00:53,083 --> 00:00:57,208
"It's this year's greatest
super-romance novel!" Well, dang!

13
00:00:57,208 --> 00:01:02,083
So you're one of those sweets-for-brains
who read romance novels, Ayaka-tan?

14
00:01:02,125 --> 00:01:04,083
I-Is that a problem?

15
00:01:04,125 --> 00:01:07,041
Bah! Is this for real?
Where's the line breaks?

16
00:01:09,166 --> 00:01:14,125
This wondrous mountain view helps expand our
imagination of things outside our daily life.

17
00:01:15,083 --> 00:01:18,041
You should take a good
look at it as well, Itsuki.

18
00:01:19,083 --> 00:01:21,083
I know, Sis.

19
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:24,083
Ah, what should I do?

20
00:01:24,208 --> 00:01:27,083
We were on the bus
for a school field trip.

21
00:01:27,125 --> 00:01:29,208
Oyamada was excited and
teasing our class president.

22
00:01:30,083 --> 00:01:35,083
Our other classmates kept their heads
down while the "elites" laughed away.

23
00:01:35,166 --> 00:01:39,208
The only ones acting normal were the
Takao sisters and our apathetic teacher.

24
00:01:40,083 --> 00:01:45,000
If I made a noble attempt to intervene,
I'd probably look pretty cool.

25
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:48,166
But having "air" like me step in would amount
to little more than a gentle breeze.

26
00:01:48,166 --> 00:01:50,083
Total effect: zero. Nothing.

27
00:01:50,125 --> 00:01:52,000
Insubstantial. Fruitless.

28
00:01:52,166 --> 00:01:54,208
Oyamada-kun, cut it out already!

29
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:58,125
Like I said, I'll give it back
if you gimme your R@IN info.

30
00:01:59,041 --> 00:02:01,041
Hey, Oyamada. Just give it back to her.

31
00:02:02,125 --> 00:02:03,125
Huh?

32
00:02:03,208 --> 00:02:04,166
Huh?

33
00:02:05,083 --> 00:02:09,000
Mimori Touka-kun, huh? Um, so...

34
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:10,041
What is it, huh?

35
00:02:10,125 --> 00:02:11,208
What's gotten into you?

36
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:15,083
I mean, look at her.
Sogou-san seems genuinely upset over it.

37
00:02:15,083 --> 00:02:16,125
- So...
- Huh?

38
00:02:16,125 --> 00:02:20,125
S-S-S-So cool! Way too cool!

39
00:02:20,166 --> 00:02:22,208
Huh? Hmm? Seriously, what is this?

40
00:02:22,208 --> 00:02:24,166
An "air-man" finally staging a revolt?

41
00:02:24,166 --> 00:02:26,041
Mimori-kun?

42
00:02:26,166 --> 00:02:28,125
Give it back to her, Shougo.

43
00:02:29,166 --> 00:02:34,166
Forget that, Takuto. Let's kill time by teasin'
Mimori-senpai who thinks he's hot stuff now!

44
00:02:34,166 --> 00:02:37,083
No, I don't plan on doing that.

45
00:02:37,125 --> 00:02:40,000
I haven't the slightest interest in Mimori.

46
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:43,083
That's super cold, Takuto.

47
00:02:43,083 --> 00:02:46,208
Dang, man! I'm not icy enough for that.

48
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:49,208
Guess that's the difference
between you and me.

49
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:52,041
I can ignore whatever you do to Mimori,

50
00:02:52,041 --> 00:02:54,125
but give Sogou back her book.

51
00:02:54,166 --> 00:02:57,041
This little song and dance is repulsive.

52
00:02:57,083 --> 00:02:58,208
That's our Kirihara-kun.

53
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:01,041
That should put an end to it, right?

54
00:03:02,083 --> 00:03:06,041
My bad, Sogou. I got a little carried away.

55
00:03:06,083 --> 00:03:08,083
Forgive and forget, yeah?

56
00:03:13,125 --> 00:03:15,000
Hey, Yasu!

57
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:19,083
Mimori-senpai's usually air, and even he
went above and beyond to trigger an event,

58
00:03:19,083 --> 00:03:23,125
so why are you, the bottom of the
2-C cast, acting like nothing's happening?

59
00:03:23,125 --> 00:03:25,041
That's cold, you know!

60
00:03:25,125 --> 00:03:29,125
That's enough now. It won't help anyone
if you drive him to suicide.

61
00:03:29,125 --> 00:03:32,041
Yasu, if you're gonna do it,
do it when I'm not your teacher.

62
00:03:32,083 --> 00:03:34,208
Okay, I'll hold back.

63
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:39,125
He's right. That wasn't like me.
For me to do something like that...

64
00:03:40,083 --> 00:03:42,000
It must've been because of that dream.

65
00:03:43,041 --> 00:03:44,000
Thanks to Mimori-senpai, the backdrop
to my fun field trip has turned real frosty.

66
00:03:44,041 --> 00:03:47,208
- Thanks to Mimori-senpai, the backdrop
to my fun field trip has turned real frosty.
- Pierce the myriad borders to those unknown to me,

67
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:49,083
- Thanks to Mimori-senpai, the backdrop
to my fun field trip has turned real frosty.
- and summon those brave of heart and spirit.

68
00:03:49,083 --> 00:03:50,208
- People are totally raining on my parade this time.
- and summon those brave of heart and spirit.

69
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:52,000
- People are totally raining on my parade this time.
- Under the guidance of Goddess Vicius's light,
manifest here in Alion.

70
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:55,041
Under the guidance of Goddess Vicius's light,
manifest here in Alion.

71
00:03:55,041 --> 00:03:56,041
- Huh? Where are we?
- Under the guidance of Goddess Vicius's light,
manifest here in Alion.

72
00:03:56,041 --> 00:03:57,208
- Huh? Where are we?
- Is this a dream?

73
00:03:58,000 --> 00:03:59,083
Some kind of prank?

74
00:03:59,083 --> 00:04:00,166
What is all this?

75
00:04:00,208 --> 00:04:03,125
You are our only hope
of striking down evil.

76
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:06,166
Welcome, heroes from another world.

77
00:04:06,208 --> 00:04:10,208
I am the goddess, Vicius. I welcome you all.

78
00:04:14,083 --> 00:04:18,125
THE GODDESS ANNOUNCING HER SUMMONS
- Here in Alion, whenever the vast evil
known as the Great Demon Empire appears,

79
00:04:19,041 --> 00:04:21,125
we summon heroes from another world.

80
00:04:22,041 --> 00:04:27,083
Roughly 200 years ago, the efforts of
the heroes saw this grand evil defeated,

81
00:04:27,083 --> 00:04:30,208
but after a long time, the Great
Demon Empire has resurfaced once more.

82
00:04:31,166 --> 00:04:33,125
You are the chosen heroes.

83
00:04:33,125 --> 00:04:37,125
So please, will you lend us
your power once more?

84
00:04:37,208 --> 00:04:39,083
So we're in another world?

85
00:04:39,125 --> 00:04:41,208
- Seems so?
- Idiot. It's just a dream.

86
00:04:41,208 --> 00:04:43,166
I don't understand any of this.

87
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:46,125
Wait, we were on the bus, yeah? Have we died?

88
00:04:46,125 --> 00:04:50,000
It must be some prank, right? Though
I'm not getting any signal on my phone.

89
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:52,125
Where's our luggage? I can't do my makeup.

90
00:04:52,125 --> 00:04:55,041
Everyone, calm down. Your teacher's here, too.

91
00:04:55,041 --> 00:04:57,083
I don't know what's going on
right now, either.

92
00:04:57,125 --> 00:05:00,125
So for now, let's listen to
this goddess's explanation.

93
00:05:00,208 --> 00:05:03,125
Thank you very much, Mr. Teacher.

94
00:05:07,166 --> 00:05:09,125
A spacious room built out of stone.

95
00:05:10,041 --> 00:05:11,208
Ancient-style fire baskets.

96
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:13,208
Soldiers wielding swords and spears.

97
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:17,083
And a goddess with golden eyes.

98
00:05:20,125 --> 00:05:22,083
Is this really some other world, then?

99
00:05:22,166 --> 00:05:26,208
Basically, you want us to defeat this
Great Demon Empire or whatever it's called?

100
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:28,083
That is the case, yes.

101
00:05:28,208 --> 00:05:31,041
And if we don't help you?

102
00:05:31,083 --> 00:05:35,083
Then you'll never be able
to return to your world.

103
00:05:35,083 --> 00:05:37,041
Is there a way to return?

104
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:42,208
The reverse summoning ritual requires
a special element known as demon king essence.

105
00:05:43,083 --> 00:05:47,000
Currently, there are only two
known methods for obtaining it.

106
00:05:47,125 --> 00:05:52,125
One is to obtain the heart of the demon king,
the source of demon king essence.

107
00:05:52,166 --> 00:05:57,125
The other is to collect the demon king essence
released upon the defeat of the demon king

108
00:05:57,166 --> 00:06:00,125
in the crystal on this necklace.

109
00:06:00,166 --> 00:06:03,083
That's all very convenient for you!

110
00:06:03,125 --> 00:06:07,000
No, screw you! This "Great Demon Empire"
has nothing to do with us!

111
00:06:10,083 --> 00:06:15,000
Would you please save our world,
O heroes of salvation?

112
00:06:15,125 --> 00:06:18,125
U-Um, may I ask a few questions?

113
00:06:18,166 --> 00:06:19,125
Go ahead.

114
00:06:19,166 --> 00:06:21,208
I-I'm Sogou Ayaka.

115
00:06:22,125 --> 00:06:25,041
You are well-mannered, Miss Sogou.

116
00:06:25,125 --> 00:06:27,083
What is your question?

117
00:06:27,083 --> 00:06:30,166
A-As you can see,
we're all just ordinary humans.

118
00:06:30,208 --> 00:06:35,208
You want us to be your "heroes of salvation,"
but I can't see how we have the power to help.

119
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:37,000
Don't worry.

120
00:06:37,166 --> 00:06:41,083
You all possess powers
that other humans do not.

121
00:06:41,166 --> 00:06:43,083
- B-But we've had no indication of that.
- Why does something feel off?

122
00:06:43,125 --> 00:06:44,208
- Why does something feel off?
- Yes, I'm sure you didn't.

123
00:06:44,208 --> 00:06:48,000
Not before you were summoned here. Bring it.

124
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:48,208
Yes, ma'am.

125
00:06:49,041 --> 00:06:52,083
Another world? Hah.
This is just some prank, right?

126
00:06:52,125 --> 00:06:54,166
I'm gettin' sick of all these lame jokes.

127
00:06:55,041 --> 00:06:56,125
That goddess...

128
00:06:56,166 --> 00:06:58,041
Is something happening?

129
00:06:58,041 --> 00:06:59,125
Huh? What's this?

130
00:06:59,125 --> 00:07:00,083
What?

131
00:07:00,125 --> 00:07:01,166
I'm kind of scared.

132
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:03,041
What is that?

133
00:07:03,041 --> 00:07:04,000
A monster?

134
00:07:18,208 --> 00:07:20,208
O holy flame that drives away evil.

135
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:24,208
In the name of the goddess, Vicius,
I command you to burn this evil to cinders.

136
00:07:25,041 --> 00:07:26,125
Fireball.

137
00:07:30,041 --> 00:07:31,083
Minamino-san!

138
00:07:32,041 --> 00:07:38,083
I see. Viewing this world as different from
our own, possibly even as a different planet,

139
00:07:38,083 --> 00:07:40,125
seems the optimal choice at present.

140
00:07:40,125 --> 00:07:45,041
Come, heroes. It is time to reveal
the skills hidden within you.

141
00:07:45,125 --> 00:07:47,083
Please come this way, one at a time.

142
00:07:53,166 --> 00:07:55,083
You have talent.

143
00:08:07,208 --> 00:08:10,083
Oh? Light this great means...

144
00:08:10,083 --> 00:08:12,083
Now, this is wonderful!

145
00:08:12,083 --> 00:08:16,000
I don't really get it,
but I got great results! So hot!

146
00:08:16,041 --> 00:08:18,208
This world ain't so bad!
A hot wind's blowin' my way!

147
00:08:20,083 --> 00:08:22,000
He's so full of himself.

148
00:08:22,083 --> 00:08:26,166
Oh! I-Impossible!

149
00:08:27,166 --> 00:08:31,166
Th-The Appraisal Crystal shattered!

150
00:08:32,166 --> 00:08:34,125
Was that something amazing just now?

151
00:08:35,166 --> 00:08:37,208
How wonderful, Sir Kirihara.

152
00:08:37,208 --> 00:08:40,000
You're the ultimate rank: S-Class!

153
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:41,041
Whoa!

154
00:08:41,041 --> 00:08:43,166
You use our alphabet in your world?

155
00:08:43,166 --> 00:08:48,000
The translator optimizes it
for your ease of understanding.

156
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:49,166
Then, what does the "S" mean?

157
00:08:49,208 --> 00:08:51,083
The "S" stands for "Special."

158
00:08:51,125 --> 00:08:54,041
So what class am I? I'm hot stuff, right?

159
00:08:54,083 --> 00:08:56,000
You're A-Class, Sir Oyamada.

160
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:58,166
Tsk. Guess there's no beating Takuto.

161
00:09:02,041 --> 00:09:04,000
What in the world?

162
00:09:04,041 --> 00:09:06,125
Oh, my! You're also S-Class, Miss Sogou!

163
00:09:07,125 --> 00:09:09,083
Another A-Class!

164
00:09:12,041 --> 00:09:13,000
What's this?

165
00:09:13,041 --> 00:09:15,000
A third S-Class?

166
00:09:15,041 --> 00:09:18,083
We're lucky to get even one
in a single summoning.

167
00:09:18,083 --> 00:09:22,000
These are the best summoning
results we've ever had!

168
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:24,041
Now, next up, it's...

169
00:09:25,125 --> 00:09:28,000
M-Mimori Touka.

170
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:29,208
Go ahead, Sir Mimori.

171
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:34,125
Purple?

172
00:09:34,125 --> 00:09:38,125
Also, isn't my light the
weakest of everyone's so far?

173
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:40,166
Okay, next, please.

174
00:09:41,125 --> 00:09:42,208
Next, please.

175
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:44,208
U-Um, what class am I?

176
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:46,083
Next!

177
00:09:46,166 --> 00:09:48,083
She's ignoring me.

178
00:09:48,083 --> 00:09:50,000
She's pretending I don't exist.

179
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:54,208
Like I'm a background character. I guess
even in another world, I get treated like air?

180
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:59,000
Well, that's reality for you. I can't become
anyone special, even in this other world.

181
00:09:59,166 --> 00:10:02,166
Yeah, that's just Mimori Touka.

182
00:10:03,041 --> 00:10:04,125
I'm fine with that.

183
00:10:06,125 --> 00:10:08,208
We've seen this reaction in the past.

184
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:12,041
It's the same as that of the dark hero,
reputed to be the strongest of all.

185
00:10:13,125 --> 00:10:15,125
We have a bountiful crop this time.

186
00:10:16,041 --> 00:10:18,041
I knew it.

187
00:10:18,041 --> 00:10:20,208
I knew my time was coming.

188
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:25,083
Okay, everyone, have you memorized
how to confirm your stats?

189
00:10:25,125 --> 00:10:26,208
Stats: Open.

190
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:30,208
Looking at it now,
these numbers seem unusually low.

191
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:34,041
The Status Adjustment Value
represents the numerical value of the boost

192
00:10:34,083 --> 00:10:35,125
to your physical abilities.

193
00:10:35,166 --> 00:10:39,208
The screen is designed in a way
that should be familiar to you as well.

194
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:42,208
As a goddess, I can do these things for you.

195
00:10:43,125 --> 00:10:46,125
Unique Skill: Inflict Status Ailments?

196
00:10:46,125 --> 00:10:50,125
Unique skills are special skills
that only that individual can use.

197
00:10:50,125 --> 00:10:52,125
Some of you may already
possess innate ones,

198
00:10:52,166 --> 00:10:54,208
but there are others you can awaken later,

199
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:56,166
so please don't worry too much.

200
00:10:57,083 --> 00:11:00,041
That's enough explanations now, goddess.

201
00:11:00,041 --> 00:11:03,041
Hey, Oyamada. Watch how
you talk to the goddess.

202
00:11:03,041 --> 00:11:07,000
You're just a D-Class hero. You think
you can talk to an A-Class hero like that?

203
00:11:07,083 --> 00:11:10,208
You're always so condescending to us,
Teach, but you stand below us now.

204
00:11:10,208 --> 00:11:12,125
Must be giving you chills.

205
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:16,125
Now, we have one more
important ritual to conduct.

206
00:11:17,208 --> 00:11:19,208
Sir Touka Mimori, please come this way.

207
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:21,125
Huh? Who, me?

208
00:11:21,125 --> 00:11:23,125
- Did I do something?
- Just shut up and go.

209
00:11:23,125 --> 00:11:29,125
Touka Mimori, you are E-Class,
the lowest rank of all the heroes here.

210
00:11:29,125 --> 00:11:34,166
In the past, the lowest-ranked heroes
have always dragged down the stronger ones.

211
00:11:34,166 --> 00:11:41,041
So after a certain point, it was decided
we would start dealing with such heroes.

212
00:11:43,125 --> 00:11:45,041
"Dealing" with?

213
00:11:45,208 --> 00:11:47,208
Yes, dealing with them.

214
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:52,125
However, suddenly dealing with them on the
spot often comes as a shock to other heroes,

215
00:11:52,125 --> 00:11:55,083
even causing them
to fight amongst themselves.

216
00:11:55,083 --> 00:12:01,083
So it was decided we would grant
even the lowest-ranked hero a chance.

217
00:12:01,166 --> 00:12:03,041
What do you mean by that?

218
00:12:03,083 --> 00:12:08,000
That teleportation circle transports
the lowest-ranked hero to a set of ruins.

219
00:12:08,166 --> 00:12:13,208
If they survive the ruins and reach
the surface, we interfere no more.

220
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:17,125
Alion grants that person
the right to live freely.

221
00:12:17,125 --> 00:12:19,041
Are these ruins dangerous?

222
00:12:19,083 --> 00:12:23,125
Who can say? We've sent many criminals
deemed highly dangerous

223
00:12:23,166 --> 00:12:26,125
and a great number of heroes
to these ruins in the past.

224
00:12:27,041 --> 00:12:33,000
Well, I suppose I'll make an exception
and tell you the name of the ruins.

225
00:12:33,125 --> 00:12:35,166
They are known as...

226
00:12:35,166 --> 00:12:37,125
the Ruins of Disposal.

227
00:12:38,083 --> 00:12:39,208
Disposal?

228
00:12:40,083 --> 00:12:41,166
What does that mean?

229
00:12:41,166 --> 00:12:43,166
Wait! Goddess!

230
00:12:43,166 --> 00:12:45,041
I have a unique skill!

231
00:12:45,083 --> 00:12:46,041
What about it?

232
00:12:46,041 --> 00:12:48,125
Mine is the skill: "Inflict Status Ailment"!

233
00:12:48,166 --> 00:12:51,000
It allows me to inflict
paralysis, poison, and—

234
00:12:52,041 --> 00:12:53,125
Listen up.

235
00:12:53,208 --> 00:12:59,166
In this world, status ailment spells
and skills are generally worthless.

236
00:13:00,125 --> 00:13:02,166
All of them have too low a success rate.

237
00:13:02,166 --> 00:13:05,166
Even when they succeed,
they barely affect low-ranked monsters,

238
00:13:05,208 --> 00:13:09,166
let alone middle-ranked ones,
and their duration is far too short.

239
00:13:09,208 --> 00:13:11,083
N-No way!

240
00:13:11,125 --> 00:13:15,041
In short, your skill is trash-tier.

241
00:13:15,083 --> 00:13:16,166
Trash-tier?

242
00:13:17,125 --> 00:13:20,125
Worse yet, it's probably
because you're E-Class,

243
00:13:20,125 --> 00:13:22,125
but your stats are also too low.

244
00:13:22,166 --> 00:13:26,041
Even if you level up, you shouldn't
expect much growth in those values.

245
00:13:26,041 --> 00:13:27,083
Are we done here?

246
00:13:27,083 --> 00:13:32,208
But you're the one who summoned me and
made me a hero. Now you're disposing of me?

247
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:34,083
- That's just completely—
- Now you're just being disgraceful.

248
00:13:34,125 --> 00:13:36,166
Now you're just being disgraceful. Hurry up and finish this.

249
00:13:37,083 --> 00:13:39,083
- The girls are all tired.
Don't you feel bad for them?
- Read the room, Mimori!

250
00:13:39,083 --> 00:13:41,041
- Kirihara-kun's so kind!
- He's the air in the room, so he can't.

251
00:13:41,083 --> 00:13:42,125
- He's the air in the room, so he can't.
- That's our S-Class!

252
00:13:42,125 --> 00:13:43,166
- That's our S-Class!
- Nice one.
- Hurry it up!

253
00:13:43,208 --> 00:13:45,166
Are you okay, Mimori?

254
00:13:52,208 --> 00:13:54,041
Y-Yasu?

255
00:13:54,083 --> 00:13:55,041
Huh?

256
00:13:55,083 --> 00:13:57,083
What do you think you're saying?

257
00:13:57,125 --> 00:13:59,000
Huh? What?

258
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:00,125
It's Yasu-"san," right?

259
00:14:00,166 --> 00:14:06,000
You're the lowest-ranked E-Class, so you need
to show more respect to an A-Class like me.

260
00:14:06,166 --> 00:14:13,083
Well, do your best to live with what
little time you have left, Mr. Trash Hero.

261
00:14:14,208 --> 00:14:17,125
Now, let's begin the ritual.

262
00:14:19,083 --> 00:14:22,208
When you're summoned,
every hero is granted a unique item.

263
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:26,166
That pathetic-looking
leather bag is your unique item.

264
00:14:26,208 --> 00:14:29,125
When you pour magic into the gem, it'll glow.

265
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:31,083
- Though all it does is glow.
- Please wait! This is all wrong!

266
00:14:31,125 --> 00:14:33,041
Please wait! This is all wrong!

267
00:14:33,083 --> 00:14:35,083
Mimori-kun is our classmate, isn't he?

268
00:14:35,125 --> 00:14:36,125
The S-Class...

269
00:14:36,125 --> 00:14:39,083
This is unforgivable!
We should release him right away—

270
00:14:46,125 --> 00:14:48,000
Sogou?

271
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:53,208
Now, everyone. Please burn the sight
of this Trash Hero onto your eyelids.

272
00:14:54,000 --> 00:14:56,125
This is the end that awaits the have-nots.

273
00:14:56,166 --> 00:14:59,000
Or, to put in your world's terms, the losers.

274
00:14:59,041 --> 00:15:02,041
However, you are all winners.

275
00:15:02,083 --> 00:15:05,125
Only a tragic fate awaits losers.

276
00:15:05,125 --> 00:15:07,083
You asshole.

277
00:15:07,125 --> 00:15:08,083
Oh?

278
00:15:09,125 --> 00:15:11,000
Paralyze!

279
00:15:12,166 --> 00:15:15,125
How insolent. That was never
going to work on a goddess.

280
00:15:16,041 --> 00:15:19,125
I have a Dispel Bubble
protective barrier active constantly.

281
00:15:19,166 --> 00:15:23,166
It automatically provides total
defense against status ailment spells.

282
00:15:23,208 --> 00:15:29,041
Everyone, this is your E-Class loser.
Your trash hero.

283
00:15:29,166 --> 00:15:31,041
Draconic Buster.

284
00:15:37,083 --> 00:15:39,125
Looks like I can use mine.

285
00:15:39,125 --> 00:15:41,083
I was just giving it a quick test run.

286
00:15:41,083 --> 00:15:42,125
Sorry about that.

287
00:15:43,041 --> 00:15:45,083
Please be more careful in the future.

288
00:15:45,166 --> 00:15:46,125
Now then.

289
00:15:49,041 --> 00:15:51,041
Later, Bottom Hero.

290
00:15:52,083 --> 00:15:55,000
Mimori Touka. R.I.P.

291
00:15:55,041 --> 00:15:58,000
Air shouldn't be wasting my precious time.

292
00:15:58,041 --> 00:15:59,000
If you're going to disappear,
hurry up and do it.

293
00:15:59,041 --> 00:16:00,083
- If you're going to disappear,
hurry up and do it.
- Damn it all.

294
00:16:00,083 --> 00:16:01,041
Damn it all.

295
00:16:01,208 --> 00:16:03,125
They're all scum.

296
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:12,000
Do you have any last words?

297
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:20,208
Why are you crying?

298
00:16:24,083 --> 00:16:25,208
You understand, don't you?

299
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:30,125
No matter how much you repress it
and pretend to be a harmless person,

300
00:16:30,166 --> 00:16:32,000
that's nothing like your true self.

301
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:33,125
- that's nothing like your true self.
- Enough. It doesn't matter.

302
00:16:33,166 --> 00:16:34,166
Enough. It doesn't matter.

303
00:16:34,166 --> 00:16:35,166
You're frustrated.

304
00:16:36,125 --> 00:16:39,125
Show them your true colors.

305
00:16:39,208 --> 00:16:43,166
Show them the true self
you've been suppressing this whole time.

306
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:48,041
Go to hell, you lousy goddess.

307
00:16:56,125 --> 00:17:00,000
If I make it back alive,
you'd better be ready for me.

308
00:17:06,166 --> 00:17:08,125
Stats: Open.

309
00:17:08,125 --> 00:17:11,208
Unable to open because
your vision is obscured.

310
00:17:14,166 --> 00:17:16,125
Oh, there it is.

311
00:17:16,125 --> 00:17:18,208
I just pour magic into this, right?

312
00:17:19,125 --> 00:17:20,125
Like this?

313
00:17:22,041 --> 00:17:25,000
It really does feel like I'm using magic.

314
00:17:25,166 --> 00:17:28,125
This feels more like a cave
than a set of ruins.

315
00:17:30,125 --> 00:17:33,083
A broken skull? It was split in two?

316
00:17:33,166 --> 00:17:35,083
What did that?

317
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:40,208
That's obvious. Something in these ruins.

318
00:17:53,125 --> 00:17:58,000
Our levels, our essence, and our hostility
are just too different! I'm shivering!

319
00:17:58,041 --> 00:18:00,125
So th-this is genuine hostility?

320
00:18:01,208 --> 00:18:03,125
This is just giving me away!

321
00:18:04,083 --> 00:18:07,000
Follow your instincts and run!
I don't want to die!

322
00:18:07,125 --> 00:18:08,166
I'm crying again.

323
00:18:08,208 --> 00:18:10,166
I'm not happy or sad.

324
00:18:10,166 --> 00:18:12,041
I'm just scared!

325
00:18:17,041 --> 00:18:18,041
Huh?

326
00:18:18,125 --> 00:18:21,000
No, that's not it. I'm not scared.

327
00:18:27,041 --> 00:18:29,041
It's an emotion I only felt recently.

328
00:18:29,083 --> 00:18:32,166
That's right. I'm not scared. Damn it all.

329
00:18:35,041 --> 00:18:38,083
I'm frustrated.

330
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:42,125
This is how Mimori Touka meets his end.

331
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:46,041
I have no weapons.
My stats are trash. My skill is major trash.

332
00:18:46,083 --> 00:18:47,083
Checkmate.

333
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:50,166
Out of options.

334
00:18:50,166 --> 00:18:53,208
- Hurry up and finish this.
- Read the room, Mimori.
- He's the air in the room, so he can't.

335
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:56,041
I want power.

336
00:18:58,041 --> 00:18:59,083
Paralyze!

337
00:19:02,083 --> 00:19:03,041
Huh?

338
00:19:05,166 --> 00:19:07,083
It actually worked?

339
00:19:08,125 --> 00:19:14,166
But that goddess said status ailments
rarely worked, even on low-ranked monsters.

340
00:19:14,166 --> 00:19:16,083
Is a minotaur a low-ranked one?

341
00:19:16,125 --> 00:19:19,083
No, it's not. Then, was it a miracle?

342
00:19:19,083 --> 00:19:21,083
Did I just get lucky with it?

343
00:19:23,166 --> 00:19:25,000
That must be it.

344
00:19:33,125 --> 00:19:34,125
I can feel it.

345
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:37,166
Genuine, unadulterated,
unfiltered hostility.

346
00:19:37,208 --> 00:19:40,166
Is it killing to eat? To survive?

347
00:19:40,208 --> 00:19:42,041
I don't know.

348
00:19:42,083 --> 00:19:44,125
Either way, it's hostility.

349
00:19:44,208 --> 00:19:46,083
A bird monster?

350
00:19:46,083 --> 00:19:48,125
Like a cockatrice or something?

351
00:19:49,125 --> 00:19:50,083
No way.

352
00:19:50,125 --> 00:19:51,166
I don't want to die!

353
00:19:51,208 --> 00:19:54,083
I don't want to die!
I don't want to die! I don't want to die!

354
00:19:54,166 --> 00:19:56,166
I don't want to die!

355
00:19:56,166 --> 00:19:58,083
Paralyze.

356
00:20:00,166 --> 00:20:03,041
It worked? So it wasn't a miracle?

357
00:20:03,041 --> 00:20:08,083
What if my skill working a second time
wasn't a miracle, but inevitable?

358
00:20:08,125 --> 00:20:12,166
What if my status ailment skill
is something completely different

359
00:20:12,166 --> 00:20:14,125
from similar magic in this world?

360
00:20:14,125 --> 00:20:16,041
Stats: Open.

361
00:20:16,083 --> 00:20:17,166
I don't have any MP left.

362
00:20:17,208 --> 00:20:21,125
I used this skill once each on the
goddess, the minotaur, and this thing.

363
00:20:21,166 --> 00:20:23,125
I also charged my leather bag twice.

364
00:20:23,208 --> 00:20:27,166
So all that's left is my own MP
outside of the stats adjustments.

365
00:20:28,083 --> 00:20:30,166
If that's not enough
for me to use my skill...

366
00:20:30,166 --> 00:20:32,083
then I'm done for.

367
00:20:33,041 --> 00:20:34,083
Poison.

368
00:20:36,125 --> 00:20:38,083
I used it!

369
00:20:38,125 --> 00:20:40,083
And I can stack it with Paralyze...

370
00:20:40,166 --> 00:20:45,125
If my success rate is incredibly high,
regardless of the monster's rank...

371
00:20:45,125 --> 00:20:48,041
and if the duration is incredibly long...

372
00:20:48,083 --> 00:20:49,125
If that's true, then...

373
00:20:57,125 --> 00:20:58,208
What?

374
00:20:59,083 --> 00:21:01,166
You were trying to kill me, too, you know.

375
00:21:03,041 --> 00:21:05,125
Is this because I used my own MP?

376
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:09,083
What'll happen if I keep using
my status ailment skill like this?

377
00:21:13,166 --> 00:21:14,208
The minotaur!

378
00:21:15,083 --> 00:21:17,208
Guess the effect of that
first Paralyze ran out.

379
00:21:20,208 --> 00:21:23,083
You're trying to kill me, too, aren't you?

380
00:21:25,125 --> 00:21:27,041
Can't fault the attempt.

381
00:21:27,083 --> 00:21:32,041
But wouldn't the normal cliché be
for someone to come to my rescue now?

382
00:21:33,083 --> 00:21:37,166
I hope you at least earn yourself
a grisly death, Touka Mimori!

383
00:21:37,208 --> 00:21:40,125
Screw you!

384
00:21:45,041 --> 00:21:47,208
I'll kill you.

385
00:21:52,083 --> 00:21:55,083
I'm not a hero or a heroine.

386
00:21:55,125 --> 00:21:59,000
I'm a background character.
No one's coming to my rescue.

387
00:21:59,125 --> 00:22:00,208
So I'll kill to survive!

388
00:22:01,000 --> 00:22:03,166
Don't rely on others. Don't count on
or expect anything from others.

389
00:22:05,166 --> 00:22:09,000
I'll conquer it all!

390
00:22:12,083 --> 00:22:15,083
Now, let's begin...

391
00:22:16,083 --> 00:22:18,125
...my fight for survival!

392
00:24:10,166 --> 00:24:14,208
THE RUINS OF DISPOSAL

